From: LPM Linux Toolchain Team <toolchain@lpm-linux.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] x86: experimentally raise znver2 and znver3 branch cost

Use the modern Zen branch-misprediction scale for znver2 and znver3 as an
LPM experiment.  Their existing value predates GCC's 2026 reconsideration of
the same cost for modern x86 and for znver4/5 specifically.

This patch requires A/B validation on Renoir before it becomes part of the
stable LPM toolchain.  It is isolated so distributions can omit it while
retaining the upstream-derived znver4/5 patch.

---
 gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h b/gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h
--- a/gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h
+++ b/gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h
@@ -1933 +1933 @@ struct processor_costs znver2_cost = {
-  COSTS_N_INSNS (2),			/* Branch mispredict scale.  */
+  COSTS_N_INSNS (2) + 3,		/* Branch mispredict scale.  */
@@ -2082 +2082 @@ struct processor_costs znver3_cost = {
-  COSTS_N_INSNS (2),			/* Branch mispredict scale.  */
+  COSTS_N_INSNS (2) + 3,		/* Branch mispredict scale.  */
-- 
2.50.1
